WEBVTT

1
00:01:34.021 --> 00:01:35.480
Excuse me. Chief Woo.

2
00:01:36.356 --> 00:01:37.566
What is it?

3
00:01:37.649 --> 00:01:39.276
Please take a look at this.

4
00:01:39.359 --> 00:01:43.822
This is a report on the six hunters
who died in a C-rank dungeon.

5
00:01:43.906 --> 00:01:46.491
The survivors are a D-rank hunter
and an E-rank hunter.

6
00:01:46.575 --> 00:01:48.160
They must have escaped.

7
00:01:48.243 --> 00:01:49.661
It happens all the time.

8
00:01:49.745 --> 00:01:51.747
No. they didn't escape.

9
00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:53.790
they got away by killing
the boss in the dungeon.

10
00:01:54.791 --> 00:01:58.837
The D-rank hunter Yoo Jinho
had quite expensive equipment.

11
00:01:58.921 --> 00:02:00.172
It's not surprising they managed to kill...

12
00:02:00.255 --> 00:02:01.548
What are you trying to say?

13
00:02:01.632 --> 00:02:04.134
Investigate it yourself
if you think it's suspicious.

14
00:02:04.217 --> 00:02:05.385
No...

15
00:02:05.469 --> 00:02:10.641
One of the survivors
is the survivor from the double dungeon.

16
00:02:10.724 --> 00:02:12.517
Hunter Sung Jinwoo.

17
00:02:13.101 --> 00:02:13.977
Sung Jinwoo?

18
00:02:19.191 --> 00:02:23.320
And one of the six who died
is Hunter Hwang Dongsuk.

19
00:02:25.322 --> 00:02:27.991
The brother of Hunter Hwang Dongsoo?

20
00:02:29.159 --> 00:02:31.036
Then it is indeed concerning...

21
00:02:32.871 --> 00:02:33.914
I'm back.

22
00:02:33.997 --> 00:02:35.248
Welcome home.

23
00:02:36.083 --> 00:02:37.709
A gift?

24
00:02:37.793 --> 00:02:39.169
It's fried chicken.

25
00:02:39.252 --> 00:02:40.379
Did something good happen?

26
00:02:40.963 --> 00:02:43.757
I'm not sure if it's a good thing.

27
00:02:44.841 --> 00:02:47.719
I've saved up for Mom's medical bills
and our living expenses.

28
00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:51.264
My stingy brother
is actually spending money.

29
00:02:52.974 --> 00:02:53.975
{\an8}Oh. right.

30
00:02:55.435 --> 00:02:57.604
What happened last time?

31
00:02:58.605 --> 00:02:59.439
The raid mission.

32
00:02:59.523 --> 00:03:01.274
They paid you a lot. right?

33
00:03:01.358 --> 00:03:03.652
But you didn't seem to have any injuries.

34
00:03:03.735 --> 00:03:06.196
Your companions must be strong.

35
00:03:09.616 --> 00:03:11.993
Well. yeah.

36
00:03:12.077 --> 00:03:14.871
You guys killed the enemies easily. right?

37
00:03:15.956 --> 00:03:18.166
<i>Yes. easily.</i>

38
00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:19.960
<i>Regardless of the difference in strength.</i>

39
00:03:21.253 --> 00:03:25.090
<i>at that moment. I had no hesitation.</i>

40
00:03:25.632 --> 00:03:29.219
<i>Moreover. I didn't even despise them.</i>

41
00:03:30.554 --> 00:03:33.598
<i>If it were the old me.
I would have tried to run away.</i>

42
00:03:34.516 --> 00:03:36.810
<i>Has my bravery increased with my level?</i>

43
00:03:37.853 --> 00:03:40.063
<i>But my opponents aren't magic beasts.</i>

44
00:03:40.147 --> 00:03:41.231
<i>They are people.</i>

45
00:03:42.399 --> 00:03:43.775
Brother?

46
00:03:43.859 --> 00:03:46.069
Are you okay?

47
00:03:46.903 --> 00:03:50.115
I thought the clerk didn't give me
the change. but I was mistaken.

48
00:03:50.198 --> 00:03:51.324
What?

49
00:03:51.408 --> 00:03:53.702
Seriously. don't scare me.

50
00:03:58.832 --> 00:04:00.250
<i>Don't think about that now.</i>

51
00:04:00.333 --> 00:04:02.961
<i>I must keep getting
stronger for my family.</i>

52
00:04:03.045 --> 00:04:03.879
<i>And I mustn't die.</i>

53
00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:07.049
<i>If the same thing happens again.
I will do just the same.</i>

54
00:04:09.509 --> 00:04:10.552
<i>What is this?</i>

55
00:04:10.635 --> 00:04:11.887
<i>"Harmful substance..."</i>

56
00:04:14.806 --> 00:04:15.807
<i>It's detoxifying me?</i>

57
00:04:19.978 --> 00:04:20.937
I'm full.

58
00:04:22.814 --> 00:04:23.774
You're done eating?

59
00:04:23.857 --> 00:04:25.275
Then I'll eat it all up.

60
00:04:25.358 --> 00:04:27.736
Then don't complain about getting fat.

61
00:04:39.331 --> 00:04:40.624
I can't get drunk at all.

62
00:04:41.374 --> 00:04:44.711
The system's special ability
has broken down the alcohol.

63
00:04:45.212 --> 00:04:46.755
Is it the effect of some skill?

64
00:04:49.132 --> 00:04:50.383
"Blessing..."

65
00:04:51.134 --> 00:04:52.594
"Health and longevity..."

66
00:04:53.762 --> 00:04:57.891
"Injuries and immunity..."

67
00:04:58.892 --> 00:05:00.393
This is it.

68
00:05:00.477 --> 00:05:02.646
The reward for the double dungeon mission.

69
00:05:02.729 --> 00:05:05.398
So much has happened.
so I never bothered to check.

70
00:05:06.233 --> 00:05:09.444
<i>Is this why my limbs could regenerate?</i>

71
00:05:10.445 --> 00:05:12.489
There are many things I'm unclear about.

72
00:05:18.245 --> 00:05:19.412
Brother.

73
00:05:19.496 --> 00:05:21.623
Someone named Yoo Jinho called for you.

74
00:05:24.751 --> 00:05:25.585
I'll be right there.

75
00:05:27.045 --> 00:05:29.673
You've had too much to drink.
Alcohol is poison to the body.

76
00:05:29.756 --> 00:05:31.299
I'm fine.

77
00:05:34.553 --> 00:05:36.596
Even if I became a doctor.
I wouldn't treat you.

78
00:05:37.931 --> 00:05:40.433
Sorry for suddenly calling you out.

79
00:05:40.517 --> 00:05:42.519
I didn't expect to see you again.

80
00:05:42.602 --> 00:05:44.187
I'm really happy.

81
00:05:44.271 --> 00:05:46.398
You saved me after all. Jinwoo.

82
00:05:46.481 --> 00:05:50.193
Thanks for giving me the magic gem too.
You helped a lot.

83
00:05:51.444 --> 00:05:52.821
And.

84
00:05:52.904 --> 00:05:54.698
you didn't reveal what happened.

85
00:05:55.907 --> 00:05:59.536
Well. they tried
to kill us first. didn't they?

86
00:06:00.078 --> 00:06:01.204
It was self-defense.

87
00:06:02.706 --> 00:06:04.624
So. why did you want me?

88
00:06:06.418 --> 00:06:08.295
I plan to build an attack team...

89
00:06:08.378 --> 00:06:09.337
I refuse.

90
00:06:09.421 --> 00:06:11.631
Huh? Well...

91
00:06:11.715 --> 00:06:12.799
At least hear me out first.

92
00:06:13.383 --> 00:06:15.844
I'm not interested
in hanging out with a rich guy.

93
00:06:16.928 --> 00:06:18.930
Twenty missions! No...

94
00:06:19.014 --> 00:06:20.891
Just 19 missions!

95
00:06:20.974 --> 00:06:22.684
Nineteen missions?

96
00:06:22.767 --> 00:06:24.269
You want to be a guild master?

97
00:06:24.853 --> 00:06:26.563
Please let me finish first.

98
00:06:26.646 --> 00:06:27.480
Please.

99
00:06:32.986 --> 00:06:34.321
Go on then.

100
00:06:36.281 --> 00:06:37.365
Yes.

101
00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:40.410
As you speculated.

102
00:06:40.493 --> 00:06:43.288
I want to obtain a guild master's license.

103
00:06:43.371 --> 00:06:45.081
And one of the conditions

104
00:06:45.165 --> 00:06:48.084
is to participate
in 20 raid missions as a hunter.

105
00:06:48.168 --> 00:06:50.086
The last mission was my first one.

106
00:06:50.962 --> 00:06:53.590
To take over the company.
I've studied hard.

107
00:06:53.673 --> 00:06:55.592
I'm confident about the written exam.

108
00:06:55.675 --> 00:06:56.509
But...

109
00:06:57.093 --> 00:06:58.219
The real combat...

110
00:06:59.804 --> 00:07:02.349
Aren't you the second young master
of Yoojin Construction?

111
00:07:03.224 --> 00:07:05.894
{\an8}I'm also doing this for our company.

112
00:07:06.394 --> 00:07:09.314
{\an8}Honestly. my father
wants to establish a guild.

113
00:07:09.397 --> 00:07:11.608
Yoojin Construction
wants to establish a guild?

114
00:07:11.691 --> 00:07:12.776
Yes.

115
00:07:14.319 --> 00:07:19.241
<i>Dungeons are certainly dangerous.
but they contain many rare treasures.</i>

116
00:07:19.908 --> 00:07:23.245
<i>Magic gems and mana crystals
are just a part of it.</i>

117
00:07:23.328 --> 00:07:26.456
<i>The bodies of high-rank beasts
can be used as materials for equipment.</i>

118
00:07:27.499 --> 00:07:31.044
<i>One can say that everything
in the dungeon can be monetized.</i>

119
00:07:31.127 --> 00:07:35.632
You plan to have your own hunters conquer
the dungeons and take all the spoils.

120
00:07:35.715 --> 00:07:37.467
so as to establish
a self-sufficient system?

121
00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:39.302
That's right.

122
00:07:39.386 --> 00:07:42.097
My father plans to hire
an S-rank hunter to be the guild master

123
00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:44.140
and my brother as the vice-guild master

124
00:07:44.224 --> 00:07:45.892
to run the guild like a company.

125
00:07:45.976 --> 00:07:47.143
An S-rank hunter?

126
00:07:47.227 --> 00:07:49.145
There are only seven of them nationally.

127
00:07:49.229 --> 00:07:50.063
Yes.

128
00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:54.317
<i>Moreover. Min Byung-gu.
the only one who hasn't joined a guild.</i>

129
00:07:54.401 --> 00:07:55.652
<i>has already retired.</i>

130
00:07:55.735 --> 00:07:58.363
Are you planning
to poach from other guilds?

131
00:08:00.657 --> 00:08:02.617
I advise you not to do that.

132
00:08:02.701 --> 00:08:05.287
The guilds that you poach from
will give you trouble.

133
00:08:05.370 --> 00:08:08.540
My brother is not one of the Awakened.
so he can't be the guild master.

134
00:08:09.249 --> 00:08:12.168
So you want to gain experience
and become the guild master

135
00:08:12.252 --> 00:08:13.712
to compete with your brother?

136
00:08:14.421 --> 00:08:17.716
If you want to hide your power
and participate in missions.

137
00:08:17.799 --> 00:08:19.134
you will need companions.

138
00:08:19.217 --> 00:08:21.678
Rather than teaming up
with high-ranked hunters.

139
00:08:21.761 --> 00:08:24.347
completing the raid missions
with an E-rank hunter

140
00:08:24.431 --> 00:08:26.099
would be more convincing to my father.

141
00:08:28.143 --> 00:08:29.769
<i>He is at least B-rank...</i>

142
00:08:29.853 --> 00:08:32.022
<i>No. it might even be higher.</i>

143
00:08:32.105 --> 00:08:34.858
{\an8}<i>Teaming up with the wrong one
could be fatal.</i>

144
00:08:34.941 --> 00:08:36.026
{\an8}<i>But if it's him...</i>

145
00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:41.406
Take a look at this.

146
00:08:43.033 --> 00:08:45.327
This building is planned
to be the guild's office.

147
00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:47.746
It's currently valued at 30 billion.

148
00:08:49.289 --> 00:08:51.958
This is the reward I am offering you.

149
00:08:52.542 --> 00:08:55.795
<i>Thirty billion for 19 C-rank missions.</i>

150
00:08:55.879 --> 00:08:58.256
<i>Before. I would have accepted right away.</i>

151
00:08:58.340 --> 00:08:59.174
<i>But...</i>

152
00:09:00.008 --> 00:09:03.178
<i>If I'm the only one in the world who can
level up. that's a different story.</i>

153
00:09:03.928 --> 00:09:08.141
<i>If I keep developing like this.
someday I will be S-rank...</i>

154
00:09:08.224 --> 00:09:11.311
<i>No. maybe even higher than that.</i>

155
00:09:12.354 --> 00:09:15.607
<i>In that case. 30 billion seems trivial.</i>

156
00:09:15.690 --> 00:09:18.360
<i>More importantly. teaming up with people</i>

157
00:09:18.443 --> 00:09:22.655
<i>without understanding
the impact of leveling up</i>

158
00:09:22.739 --> 00:09:24.032
<i>is too risky.</i>

159
00:09:24.657 --> 00:09:25.658
Sorry.

160
00:09:29.788 --> 00:09:31.039
Please. wait.

161
00:09:31.998 --> 00:09:33.875
As long as you help me.

162
00:09:33.958 --> 00:09:36.211
I will keep this secret for you
for a lifetime.

163
00:09:50.558 --> 00:09:53.520
<i>I want the information
on those two survivors.</i>

164
00:09:53.603 --> 00:09:55.397
<i>Bring me their documents immediately.</i>

165
00:09:58.358 --> 00:09:59.442
Excuse me.

166
00:10:00.485 --> 00:10:01.778
I have brought the documents.

167
00:10:01.861 --> 00:10:02.695
Mr. Hwang.

168
00:10:05.824 --> 00:10:07.992
My brother was killed.

169
00:10:10.662 --> 00:10:12.038
This has not been confirmed yet...

170
00:10:12.122 --> 00:10:13.081
The documents?

171
00:10:14.749 --> 00:10:16.167
Yes. right here.

172
00:10:17.252 --> 00:10:18.378
Laura.

173
00:10:18.461 --> 00:10:20.922
what would happen
if I killed someone in another country?

174
00:10:21.798 --> 00:10:22.882
Are you serious?

175
00:10:28.763 --> 00:10:33.059
In a country with an extradition treaty
regarding hunter crimes.

176
00:10:33.143 --> 00:10:35.061
you would be prosecuted
under that country's laws.

177
00:10:35.645 --> 00:10:37.564
But if there's no extradition treaty.

178
00:10:37.647 --> 00:10:40.150
you would be subject
to the laws of our own country.

179
00:10:41.192 --> 00:10:42.485
So...

180
00:10:42.569 --> 00:10:44.362
Depending on negotiations
with the government.

181
00:10:44.446 --> 00:10:45.864
there might be leniency.

182
00:10:47.449 --> 00:10:49.617
Adjust my schedule.

183
00:10:49.701 --> 00:10:53.204
A sudden change of schedule
will affect the operation of the guild.

184
00:10:53.913 --> 00:10:55.206
What's my schedule like?

185
00:10:55.790 --> 00:10:57.333
It's fully booked for now.

186
00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:00.962
Then clear it for later.

187
00:11:01.045 --> 00:11:02.130
I understand.

188
00:11:02.630 --> 00:11:04.257
I will arrange it.

189
00:11:05.175 --> 00:11:07.385
{\an8}D-rank Hunter Yoo Jinho.

190
00:11:08.344 --> 00:11:10.513
{\an8}E-rank Hunter Sung Jinwoo.

191
00:11:13.683 --> 00:11:17.353
Don't die before then.

192
00:11:22.483 --> 00:11:25.111
It's rare to see you exercising.

193
00:11:25.195 --> 00:11:28.907
Studying all the time
is harmful to health. right?

194
00:11:29.782 --> 00:11:31.409
Not because you had
too much fried chicken?

195
00:11:39.042 --> 00:11:39.876
Hey.

196
00:11:39.959 --> 00:11:42.170
If you had 30 billion. what would you do?

197
00:11:42.253 --> 00:11:43.880
Why are you asking?

198
00:11:43.963 --> 00:11:45.256
Just a random question.

199
00:11:46.007 --> 00:11:49.844
Pay Mom's medical bills
and college tuition fees.

200
00:11:49.928 --> 00:11:50.929
And the rest?

201
00:11:52.639 --> 00:11:53.806
Save it up.

202
00:11:53.890 --> 00:11:56.184
I don't know. That's too much money.

203
00:11:57.977 --> 00:11:59.020
That's true.

204
00:11:59.979 --> 00:12:01.606
Just keep up at your own pace.

205
00:12:02.565 --> 00:12:03.942
Wait. brother!

206
00:12:07.987 --> 00:12:10.114
Even as an E-rank one.
he is still a hunter.

207
00:12:14.702 --> 00:12:15.536
Yes...

208
00:12:16.788 --> 00:12:17.664
No. don't check.

209
00:12:19.374 --> 00:12:20.750
Eleven kilometers?

210
00:12:21.542 --> 00:12:24.337
Why are the numbers exceeding
the goal also recorded?

211
00:12:29.676 --> 00:12:30.593
I see.

212
00:12:31.344 --> 00:12:33.304
Then let's see how far I can go.

213
00:12:37.642 --> 00:12:38.977
Brother...

214
00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:41.354
I finally caught up.

215
00:12:42.146 --> 00:12:43.648
I'll have another lap.

216
00:12:51.197 --> 00:12:53.241
It stopped at twice the goal.

217
00:12:53.324 --> 00:12:54.534
Then the rest...

218
00:13:02.292 --> 00:13:05.795
The daily quest became the secret quest.

219
00:13:06.796 --> 00:13:07.630
Yes.

220
00:13:08.923 --> 00:13:11.509
I can choose different boxes.

221
00:13:12.176 --> 00:13:15.471
{\an8}Guess I'll choose Blessed Random Loot Box.

222
00:13:30.111 --> 00:13:31.195
A key again?

223
00:13:33.823 --> 00:13:35.783
{\an8}"The Demon's Castle..."

224
00:13:35.867 --> 00:13:37.618
{\an8}Acquisition difficulty of an S-rank?!

225
00:13:46.336 --> 00:13:48.713
"Cures all illnesses with powerful magic."

226
00:13:49.714 --> 00:13:51.090
"Elixir of Life."

227
00:13:59.807 --> 00:14:04.812
<i>If that Elixir of Life
can really cure all illnesses...</i>

228
00:14:06.981 --> 00:14:08.107
<i>Then of course...</i>

229
00:14:16.991 --> 00:14:20.495
<i>If the acquisition difficulty of the key
is proportional to the dungeon's.</i>

230
00:14:20.578 --> 00:14:22.288
<i>I am opening an S-rank dungeon.</i>

231
00:14:23.373 --> 00:14:24.290
<i>If so.</i>

232
00:14:24.374 --> 00:14:27.210
<i>what awaits me inside will be magic beasts</i>

233
00:14:27.293 --> 00:14:30.213
<i>similar to those on Jeju Island
that even S-rank hunters can't handle.</i>

234
00:14:39.389 --> 00:14:41.849
<i>With my current strength.</i>

235
00:14:42.475 --> 00:14:44.644
<i>can I deal with beasts of that level?</i>

236
00:14:50.692 --> 00:14:52.527
<i>It'd be a lie to say I'm not scared.</i>

237
00:14:53.945 --> 00:14:55.530
<i>If things don't go well.</i>

238
00:14:55.613 --> 00:14:58.574
<i>I will use this teleportation stone
I got from the Instance dungeon.</i>

239
00:15:06.708 --> 00:15:08.418
<i>If I give up. everything is over.</i>

240
00:15:09.210 --> 00:15:12.463
<i>I need to become stronger.
to level up even higher.</i>

241
00:15:12.547 --> 00:15:13.965
<i>I must take back everything.</i>

242
00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:18.553
How could I die here?

243
00:15:40.742 --> 00:15:42.326
I can hardly inflict any damage.

244
00:15:42.410 --> 00:15:44.829
The gap is still so huge
after I use the title skills?

245
00:15:51.836 --> 00:15:52.670
No use.

246
00:16:24.535 --> 00:16:25.369
<i>A warning?</i>

247
00:16:26.037 --> 00:16:28.247
<i>A third of my HP was gone in an instant.</i>

248
00:16:35.880 --> 00:16:37.006
{\an8}<i>All abilities doubled?</i>

249
00:16:41.511 --> 00:16:42.345
<i>So fast...</i>

250
00:16:47.016 --> 00:16:48.184
<i>Only a half left?</i>

251
00:16:49.727 --> 00:16:51.145
There's no other way.

252
00:16:51.229 --> 00:16:52.271
Full Recovery!

253
00:16:57.902 --> 00:16:59.278
I stabbed it.

254
00:17:43.698 --> 00:17:45.575
<i>The warnings keep popping up.</i>

255
00:17:46.158 --> 00:17:49.704
{\an8}<i>The system issues warnings
at critical moments to prevent my death</i>

256
00:17:50.413 --> 00:17:52.039
{\an8}<i>because I am a player?</i>

257
00:17:52.874 --> 00:17:56.752
{\an8}<i>No matter what. this thing
can't be an ordinary second awakening.</i>

258
00:17:57.712 --> 00:18:00.965
{\an8}I must hold on for at least
three minutes until its skill ends...

259
00:18:01.507 --> 00:18:03.217
No. this is too dangerous.

260
00:18:05.303 --> 00:18:06.596
<i>Do I have to resort to this...</i>

261
00:18:21.068 --> 00:18:23.279
What can I do to survive?

262
00:18:24.864 --> 00:18:26.699
<i>A few more hits and I'll be dead.</i>

263
00:18:27.199 --> 00:18:28.701
<i>Is there any way...</i>

264
00:18:30.661 --> 00:18:31.662
{\an8}<i>The shop...</i>

265
00:18:31.746 --> 00:18:32.747
{\an8}<i>I completely forgot.</i>

266
00:18:35.124 --> 00:18:36.584
<i>One bottle costs 300 gold coins...</i>

267
00:18:37.084 --> 00:18:38.210
Three bottles.

268
00:18:44.383 --> 00:18:46.385
One bottle only restores 100 points of HP?

269
00:18:46.886 --> 00:18:48.137
This is simply...

270
00:18:50.348 --> 00:18:51.432
<i>Poison?</i>

271
00:18:52.141 --> 00:18:54.518
You've had too much to drink.
Alcohol is poison to the body.

272
00:18:54.602 --> 00:18:56.228
I'm fine.

273
00:18:58.230 --> 00:18:59.440
<i>I have to do this.</i>

274
00:19:17.208 --> 00:19:18.167
Okay.

275
00:19:29.136 --> 00:19:30.262
<i>It's not over yet!</i>

276
00:19:31.806 --> 00:19:33.057
<i>I can still move!</i>

277
00:19:38.145 --> 00:19:39.605
<i>Its skill effect has ended!</i>

278
00:21:29.215 --> 00:21:30.508
<i>Is this the item I obtained?</i>

279
00:21:31.509 --> 00:21:32.718
<i>Another key?</i>

280
00:21:33.302 --> 00:21:36.680
Is this the door
that Cerberus was guarding?

281
00:21:38.015 --> 00:21:38.891
What is this?

282
00:21:44.647 --> 00:21:46.982
"The pattern for the Elixir of Life"?

283
00:21:51.654 --> 00:21:54.115
<i>This experience made me understand
my current strength.</i>

284
00:21:54.615 --> 00:21:57.451
<i>Entering the castle at my current level
would surely mean death.</i>

285
00:21:58.160 --> 00:21:58.994
<i>But...</i>

286
00:21:59.995 --> 00:22:02.039
I will return in the near future.

287
00:22:02.998 --> 00:22:04.125
Definitely.
